3) and Charlie is green (fact 4).From fact 12, all green people are nice.So Charlie is nice because Charlie is green.So Charlie is nice.\n\nFrom fact 17, all nice people are blue.So if Charlie is nice, then Charlie must be blue.Therefore, Charlie is blue.So the statement "Charlie is blue" should be true.\n\nWait, but let me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything.Let\'s go through each relevant fact again.\n\nCharlie is not green (fact 4).Fact 12 says all green people are mean, so Charlie is mean.Fact 17 says all mean people are not blue, so Charlie must not be blue.That seems complex.\n\nIs there any certainty that Charlie is blue?Let\'s see.Are there any confirmations or other rules that might support this?Let\'s check the other facts.\n\nFact 15: All green, blue people are small.Wait, does this mean that if someone is green and blue, they are small?Or does it mean that all green people are small and all blue people are small?The wording is a bit clear.It says "All green, blue people are small."So maybe it\'s saying that if someone is both green and blue, they are small.But since Charlie is not green and we\'ve deduced Charlie is not blue, then Charlie would be neither green nor blue, so Charlie is small.But does that affect anything else?.\n\nWait, but from fact 14, all small people are not round.So if Charlie is small, then Charlie is not round.But we do have some information about Charlie\'s roundness, but that\'s okay because the question is about being blue, not round.\n\nAnother point: Fact 13 says if someone is warm, then they are mean.Harry is warm (fact 9) and mean (fact 10), which fits.But Charlie is not warm (fact 3), so that rule does apply to Charlie.\n\nFact 11: If someone is smooth, then they are nice.But since Charlie is mean, Charlie can be smooth.Fact 16 says if someone is not round, they are rough.Since Charlie is mean, and all mean people are not blue, and if Charlie is small (from fact 15, since Charlie is not green and not blue), then Charlie is not round (from fact 14).So Charlie is not round, which means Charlie is rough (from fact 16).That all checks out.\n\nSo, putting it all together: Charlie is not green → Charlie is mean → Charlie is not blue\n</think>\nTherefore, the option is ']] 14%|#3        | 83/600 [03:27<04:01,  2.14it/s]
