So Harry, being not red, is smooth.\n\nFrom point 12: Smooth things are cruel. So Harry, being smooth, is cruel.\n\nNow, let\'s see what else we can deduce about Harry. From point 9: All cruel things are hairless. Since Harry is cruel, he cannot be hairless.\n\nWait, but the question is whether Harry is furry. So according to this, Harry is not furry, which would make the statement "Harry is furry" true.\n\nLet me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything. Harry is small → loud → not red → smooth → cruel → not hairless. So yes, Harry is not furry. Therefore, the statement that Harry is furry is true.\n\nI don\'t think there\'s any conflicting information here. All the rules chain together to show that Harry cannot be furry.\n</think>\nTherefore, the option is ']]
