at fact 12: Rough, kind people are quiet.So, if someone is both rough and kind, they are quiet.Now, Gary is rough (fact 5) and kind (fact 4), so Gary is quiet.But that\'s about Gary, not Harry.\n\nFact 13: Old, gentle people are harsh. Harry is old (fact 7). If Harry is gentle, then he\'s harsh. But we do know if Harry is gentle yet.\n\nWait, fact 15 says furry people are gentle. Since Harry is not furry (from fact 9), he cannot be gentle. So, Harry is not gentle.\n\nNow, since Harry is old and gentle (from fact 15), according to fact 13, he cannot be harsh. So, Harry is not harsh.\n\nNow, since Harry is gentle and harsh (from fact 15 and fact 13), according to fact 12, he cannot be loud. So, Harry is loud.\n\nNow, we have Harry is not furry (from fact 9), loud (from fact 12), and harsh (from fact 13). So, from fact 10, all loud, harsh people are not furry, which we already know Harry is not.\n\nFrom fact 11, if Harry is not furry and loud, then he\'s flat. Since he is neither, he cannot be flat.\n\nBut the question is about whether Harry is furry. From fact 9, Harry is old → not furry. So, Harry is not furry. Therefore, the statement "Harry is furry" is true.\n\nWait, but let me double-check. Is there any possibility that Harry is furry? Let\'s see.\n\nFact 9 says old people are not furry. Harry is old, so he cannot be furry. There\'s no exception given, so Harry is definitely not furry.\n</think>\nTherefore, the option is ']]
