ems straightforward, right?So, Harry is furry.\n\nBut wait, let me check if there\'s any conflicting information.Let\'s see.\n\nHarry is young, so he\'s furry.Now, let\'s see if Harry is quiet.From fact 11, if Harry is furry and quiet, then he\'s round.But we don\'t know if Harry is quiet yet.Let\'s see if we can determine that.\n\nLooking at fact 12: Rough, kind people are quiet.So, if someone is both rough and kind, they are quiet.Now, Gary is rough (fact 5) and kind (fact 4), so Gary is quiet.But that\'s about Gary, not Harry.\n\nFact 13: Old, gentle people are cruel. Harry is old (fact 7). If Harry is gentle, then he\'s cruel. But we don\'t know if Harry is gentle yet.\n\nWait, fact 15 says furry people are gentle. Since Harry is not furry (from fact 9), he must be gentle. So, Harry is gentle.\n\nNow, since Harry is old and gentle (from fact 15), according to fact 13, he must be cruel. So, Harry is cruel.\n\nNow, since Harry is gentle and cruel (from fact 15 and fact 13), according to fact 12, he must be loud. So, Harry is loud.\n\nNow, we have Harry is not furry (from fact 9), loud (from fact 12), and cruel (from fact 13). So, from fact 10, all loud, cruel people are not furry, which we already know Harry is not.\n\nFrom fact 11, if Harry is not furry and loud, then he\'s flat. Since he is both, he must be flat.\n\nBut the question is about whether Harry is furry. From fact 9, Harry is old → not furry. So, Harry is not furry. Therefore, the statement "Harry is furry" is true.\n\nWait, but let me double-check. Is there any possibility that Harry is furry? Let\'s see.\n\nFact 9 says old people are not furry. Harry is old, so he must be not furry. There\'s no exception given, so Harry is definitely not furry.\n</think>\nTherefore, the option is ']]
