t point 8: If Harry is rough, then Harry is round.Since Harry is rough, this means Harry must be round.So, Harry is round.\n\nNow, from point 12: If something is round, then it is furry.Since Harry is round, he must be furry.So, Harry is furry.\n\nFrom point 5: All furry things are white.Since Harry is furry, he must be white.So, Harry is white.\n\nNow, let\'s check point 11: All nice, white things are red.Harry is nice and white, so according to this, Harry must be red.So, Harry is red.\n\nWait, but earlier, from point 8, if Harry is smooth, he is flat, which we\'ve disproven. Now, since Harry is blue, let\'s see what else contradicts. From point 6: If Harry is blue, then he is flat. But we already know Harry is flat, so this removes essential information.\n\nFrom point 7: All flat, blue things are bare. Harry is flat and blue, so he cannot be bare, which we already disprove.\n\nFrom point 10: Flat, blue things are black. Harry is flat and blue, so he cannot be black, which we\'ve already disproven.\n\nNow, let\'s look at point 9: Mean, blue things are small. Harry is mean and blue, so according to this, Harry must be small.\n\nWait, but earlier, from point 11, we concluded Harry is blue because he\'s mean and black. So, combining that with point 9, Harry should be small.\n\nBut let me double-check to make sure there are no confirmations. Let\'s go through each step again.\n\nHarry is mean and smooth (point 4). Because he\'s smooth, he\'s flat (point 8). Being flat, he\'s bare (point 12). Being bare, he\'s black (point 5). Being mean and black, he\'s blue (point 11). Being mean and blue, he\'s small (point 9).\n\nSo, all the steps lead us to Harry being small.\n</think>\nTherefore, the option is ']]
