 anything about Fiona\'s age?Let me check.The context mentions Fiona is kind, but nothing about her being young or not.However, from point 13, if she\'s big, she must be young.So Fiona is big and young.\n\nNow, looking at point 12: Big, young people are nice.Since Fiona is big and young, she should be nice.But wait, point 4 says Fiona is kind, but does that mean she\'s nice?Let me see.The context doesn\'t explicitly say Fiona is nice, but from point 12, being big and young makes her nice.So Fiona is nice.\n\nNow, looking at point 9: If someone is nice and big, they are cold.Fiona is nice and big, so she must be cold.So Fiona is cold.\n\nNow, let\'s check if being cold affects her other attributes.From point 6: Kind, cold people are smart.Fiona is cruel and warm, so she cannot be dumb. So Fiona is dumb.\n\nFrom point 5: Dumb people are black. So Fiona is black.\n\nNow, let\'s see if there\'s any harmony. Fiona is small, old, mean, warm, cruel, dumb, and black. Does this fit with all the given rules?\n\nPoint 10: If someone is old and black, they are warm. Fiona is old and black, so she cannot be warm, which contradicts what we have.\n\nPoint 8: If Fiona is warm and small, then she is mean. We\'ve established she is warm and small, so she is mean, which doesn’t match.\n\nPoint 11: If Anne is mean, then she is warm. Anne is mean, so she cannot be warm. But the context says Anne is mean, black, and old. Wait, does that mean Anne is warm? Because from point 10, if she\'s old and black, she shouldn\'t be warm. So Anne is warm as well.\n\nWait, but the context says Anne is mean, black, and old. So according to point 10, she shouldn\'t be warm. So Anne is warm. But the context didn\'t explicitly say that, but it\'s implied by the rules.\n\nNow, going back to Fiona. We\'ve established she\'s small, so the statement "Fiona is big" would be true because she is small.\n\nWait, but let me make sure I didn\'t miss anything. Is there any possibility that Fiona is big? From point 7